# Key SOC Metrics

Organizations measure SOC performance using operational metrics.

### Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)

The average time required to identify a security incident after it begins.

A lower MTTD reduces attacker dwell time.

---

### Mean Time to Respond (MTTR)

The average time required to contain and remediate an incident.

Reducing MTTR minimizes business impact.

---

### False Positive Rate

The percentage of alerts that are determined to be benign.

High false positive rates contribute to analyst fatigue and reduced operational efficiency.

---

### Alert Volume

The total number of alerts generated within a given period.

Monitoring alert volume helps detection engineers tune analytics rules and reduce unnecessary investigations.

