# Best Practices

When operating a SOC, organizations should:

- Continuously tune detection rules.
- Reduce false positives.
- Prioritize high-risk alerts.
- Use threat intelligence to enrich investigations.
- Automate repetitive tasks where appropriate.
- Conduct regular incident response exercises.
- Document lessons learned after every incident.

